{"tool_name":"scte","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"scte","home":"https://github.com/JiekaiLab/scTE","license":"MIT","summary":"scTE builds genome indices for the fast alignment of reads to genes and Transposable elements (TEs).","addition_date":"2024-07-18T11:34:53.652671Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T13:50:42.399496Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["1.0.0"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:scte","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"chen_jiekai@gibh.ac.cn","name":"Jiekai Chen","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-5168-7074","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"Jiangping He","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-1425-3530","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"cmd":"scTE_build -te TEs.bed -gene Genes.gtf -o custome\nscTE -i inp.bam -o out -x mm10.exclusive.idx --hdf5 True","input":[{"data":{"term":"Annotation track","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3002"},"format":[{"term":"BED","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3003"}]},{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid features","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1276"},"format":[{"term":"GTF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2306"}]},{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1383"},"format":[{"term":"BAM","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2572"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"RNA-Seq quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3800"},{"term":"Sequence annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0361"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Gene expression matrix","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3112"},"format":[{"term":"CSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3752"},{"term":"HDF5","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3590"}]}]}],"name":"scTE","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"billsfriend","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-021-21808-x","metadata":{"abstract":"Transposable elements (TEs) make up a majority of a typical eukaryote\u2019s genome, and contribute to cell heterogeneity in unclear ways. Single-cell sequencing technologies are powerful tools to explore cells, however analysis is typically gene-centric and TE expression has not been addressed. Here, we develop a single-cell TE processing pipeline, scTE, and report the expression of TEs in single cells in a range of biological contexts. Specific TE types are expressed in subpopulations of embryonic stem cells and are dynamically regulated during pluripotency reprogramming, differentiation, and embryogenesis. Unexpectedly, TEs are expressed in somatic cells, including human disease-specific TEs that are undetectable in bulk analyses. Finally, we apply scTE to single-cell ATAC-seq data, and demonstrate that scTE can discriminate cell type using chromatin accessibly of TEs alone. Overall, our results classify the dynamic patterns of TEs in single cells and their contributions to cell heterogeneity.","authors":[{"name":"Babarinde I.A."},{"name":"Chen J."},{"name":"Chen R."},{"name":"He J."},{"name":"Hutchins A.P."},{"name":"Li Y."},{"name":"Ma G."},{"name":"Shi J."},{"name":"Sun L."},{"name":"Wei Y."},{"name":"Xu S."},{"name":"Zhuang Q."}],"citationCount":73,"date":"2021-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Communications","title":"Identifying transposable element expression dynamics and heterogeneity during development at the single-cell level with a processing pipeline scTE"},"pmcid":"PMC7935913","pmid":"33674594","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Functional, regulatory and non-coding RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0659"},{"term":"Mobile genetic elements","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0798"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"scTE","home":"https://bio.tools/scte","license":"MIT","version":"1.0.0","summary":"scTE builds genome indices for the fast alignment of reads to genes and Transposable elements (TEs).",